# Jekyll site — commands by situation

Use these from the project root. **Pick the row that matches what the user is doing.**

| Situation | Command | Notes |
|-----------|---------|--------|
| **Local dev / preview** (layouts, CSS, JS, content; fast, no RSS) | `bundle exec jekyll serve --destination /tmp/curatedrunningpodcasts-dev --incremental --force-polling` | Skips RSS; uses `_data/latest_podcast_episodes.yml` and/or `.jekyll-rss-cache/`. `--incremental` + Sass partial deps so `_style/` edits rebuild CSS; `--force-polling` if file watch is flaky. |
| **Local full site build** (not deploying `docs/`) | `bundle exec jekyll build --destination <dir>` | Same fast path as serve unless production env set. |
| **Refresh podcast RSS locally** (test players / latest episodes) | `LOCAL_PUSH_FETCH_RSS=1 bash tools/local-push.sh "..."` or `bash tools/ci-feed-and-episode-build.sh` | RSS + YouTube match + episode HTML; slow. |
| **Before commit/push** that includes built output (`docs/`) | `bash tools/local-push.sh "Your message"` | **Preferred.** Directory-only production build (`tools/ci-directory-build.sh`): no RSS, no YouTube, no episode HTML. Retries if CI wins the race. |
| **Manual directory-only build** | `bash tools/ci-directory-build.sh` | Same as push CI: committed `_data`, `SKIP_EPISODE_PAGES=1`, finishes in minutes. |
| **Update committed episode data** (RSS + YouTube + episode pages) | CI feed workflow (every 2h) or `LOCAL_PUSH_FETCH_RSS=1 bash tools/local-push.sh "..."` | Do not run full RSS builds locally unless testing the pipeline. |

**Agent behavior**

- If the user asks to **push**, **commit and push**, **deploy**, or **ship** the site: run **`bash tools/local-push.sh "…"`** with a clear commit message. Do **not** `git pull --no-rebase` on `docs/` manually unless the script fails repeatedly.
- If the user is **only iterating locally** or asks to **run the site**: use **`bundle exec jekyll serve`** (or a non-production `jekyll build`); do not force `JEKYLL_ENV=production` unless they need production URLs.
- Do **not** run `JEKYLL_ENV=production bundle exec jekyll build --destination docs` without `SKIP_EPISODE_PAGES=1` unless explicitly regenerating all episode HTML (CI handles that).

## CI workflow split

| Workflow | When | What it does |
|----------|------|----------------|
| **Push Jekyll build** | Content/layout pushes | `ci-directory-build.sh` — fast directory pages only |
| **Feed Jekyll build** | Every 2h | RSS → YouTube match → episode pages |
| **Episode pages Jekyll build** | After feed / plugin changes | YouTube match → missing episode HTML |
| **Scheduled Jekyll build** | Daily | Same as feed (full RSS + YouTube + episode pages) |

Episode HTML, YouTube IDs, and RSS data are refreshed by CI — not by push builds or default local pushes.

## Git push checklist

1. Run: `bash tools/local-push.sh "Your commit message"`
2. Include **`docs/`** from the directory build; do **not** commit `_data/latest_podcast_episodes.yml` unless you ran `LOCAL_PUSH_FETCH_RSS=1`.
